{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 (v4.35.0) + Mathlib formalization of structural theorems, edge-dual linear-programming relaxations (Lemma W and refinements), Lemma C, local obstruction rules, unconditional counterexample lower bounds, explicit ceiling witnesses, and conditional transfer theorems for Giuga's conjecture (1950). Across 21 compared theorems (zero sorry, zero native_decide, standard axioms only), Lean 4 proves unconditionally that every Giuga counterexample has at least 578 distinct prime factors and exceeds 10^1803 (at least 1,804 decimal digits), constructs an explicit 8,135-prime normal odd prime set (40,733 digits) and an explicit 8,138-prime witness satisfying all seven local counterexample rules (40,751 digits), proves all forms of Lemma W, Lemma C, and the mod-8 count congruence, and proves conditional lifting theorems reaching >= 8,138 prime factors and > 10^40747 (>= 40,748 decimal digits) from explicit depth-6 frontier hypotheses. Main results in the companion paper: 0 of 2 headline theorems purely in Lean 4 (0%) · 2 of 2 by Lean 4 + external exact-integer certificates (all 15 prefixes below 17). Existence of a Giuga counterexample remains open. Companion working paper, exact integer checker, and prior-work search log: https://mathdiscoveries.org/results/giuga.",
